{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0127FfF3m6sqs7YT6Ycq1CaC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted experimental results for each \"planned\" experiment in the experiment_plan, under the \"worst\" tier scenario they've defined. Let me identify all experiments with status \"planned\":\n\n1. plan_001 - real_data_dif_mmlu (planned)\n2. plan_002 - rl_robustness_validation (planned)\n3. plan_003a - constat_perturbation_eval (planned)\n4. plan_003b - dvd_generation_variance_eval (planned)\n5. plan_003c - ensemble_fusion (planned)\n\n\n6. plan_004 - cross_benchmark_gsm8k (planned)\n7. plan_005 - bifactor_irt_equating_pilot (planned)\n8. plan_006 - item_generation_calibration (planned)\n9. plan_007 - cumulative_bayesian_dif (planned)\n10. plan_008 - graceful_degradation_analysis (planned)\n11. plan_009 - item_focused_trees (planned)\n12. plan_010 - architecture_stratified_dif (planned)\n13. plan_011 - semi_synthetic_contamination_validation (planned)\n14. plan_028 - multi_benchmark_temporal_dif (planned)\n\nI'm continuing to compile the full list of planned experiments to ensure I generate predictions for all of them.\n\nWait, I need to cross-check against the registry because many of these are already marked as completed. Looking at what's actually been done, I see several have DONE status including the MVP phases, the real data DIF work on MMLU, matched ability analysis, semi-synthetic validation, IRT conditioning, local independence checks, within-subject DIF studies, and bifactor IRT work. Let me verify which ones are still genuinely planned versus already executed. I'm noticing a discrepancy between the experiment_plan status and the registry entries—many experiments marked as \"planned\" in the plan actually show completion status in the registry. The user is asking for detailed predictions for all experiments listed as \"planned\" in the experiment_plan, so I should generate worst-tier predictions for each one regardless of their registry status, treating the plan as the source of truth for what needs predictions. happened; the user wants me to predict what would happen under the \"worst\" scenario.\n\nActually, re-reading more carefully - I think the task is to generate imagined/predicted results for all the planned experiments under the \"worst\" tier scenario. The registry shows actual results, but the \"worst\" tier is a hypothetical scenario where things go badly. The user wants me to imagine what the results would look like if the worst-case scenario materializes.\n\nLet me look at the worst tier definition again - it shows the metric ranges where the core psychometric framing gets fundamentally questioned and needs a complete reframe. The temporal label assignment introduces substantial spurious DIF, detection robustness drops significantly, and reviewer scores plummet. The narrative would shift away from psychometric measurement drift toward a pure empirical characterization paper.\n\nNow I'm working through each planned experiment to generate detailed predictions for what the results would look like under this worst-case scenario, including the rationale for each prediction.\n\nFor plan_001, the 31% C% signal mostly collapses when you account for temporal label assignment artifacts - permutation testing shows only 12-20% is genuine signal. The enrichment against prior work stays around 1.0, and within-family analysis reveals the high C% is driven by cohort composition rather than true measurement drift. Domain specificity turns out to be weak.\n\nFor plan_002, adding RL models causes DIF flags to shift dramatically (low Jaccard overlap of 0.3-0.55), but traditional detectors show minimal AUROC degradation (0-0.08 drop). This reveals DIF is highly sensitive to cohort composition changes, which undermines confidence in it as a reliable detector.\n\nFor plan_003a, ConStat performs reasonably on non-RL models and compares favorably to DIF on certain metrics, but I need to see what comes next to finish this thought.\n\nFor plan_003b, DVD handles variant contamination detection reasonably well and complements ConStat, further questioning whether DIF offers any unique advantage.\n\nFor plan_003c, the ensemble approach doesn't meaningfully outperform individual methods because the underlying signals are too correlated or base rates make fusion unreliable.\n\nFor plan_004, GSM8K shows much lower C% (8-14% range) compared to MMLU's 31%, GSM1K correlation is weak or reversed, and semi-synthetic replication yields smaller ΔTPR gains (0.25-0.4).\n\nFor plan_005, the bifactor IRT model fails to converge or produce meaningful equating results.\n\nFor plan_006, generated items don't correlate well with difficulty targets and student simulation calibration is poor.\n\nFor plan_007, cumulative Bayesian improvements plateau below the 0.70 power threshold even after three administrations.\n\nFor plan_008, validity degrades more rapidly than anticipated when items are replaced.\n\nFor plan_009, item-focused trees either largely replicate categorical DIF findings or reveal conflicting patterns that undermine the categorical results.\n\nFor plan_010, stratifying by architecture reveals MMLU is almost entirely decoder-based.\n\nFor plan_011, the replication shows lower ΔTPR in the 0.25-0.4 range with concerning FPR inflation.\n\nFor plan_028, DIF rates vary substantially across benchmarks (8-28%), suggesting this might be specific to MMLU rather than a general phenomenon.\n\nFor plan_029, the permutation null yields C% around 12-20%, indicating a significant portion of the observed 31% could be noise from random temporal label assignment.\n\nFor plan_030, examining odds ratios and regression transparency...\n\nNow I'm seeing that item-level models reveal confounds are actually larger than what domain-level analysis suggested, which weakens the explanatory power of the simpler approach. I need to generate comprehensive predicted results for each planned experiment under the worst-case tier, with specific metric values that align with the key indicator ranges I've defined.\n\nLooking at the experiments in the registry, I should work through each one systematically and assign worst-case predicted values. Let me structure the full YAML output with all planned experiments and their corresponding worst-tier results. Writing YAML configuration...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24168,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24168},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03381ec8-53c9-4c55-86f7-a45910704277","uuid":"cb763f59-9e9d-4bc3-8edf-a1fd47d01126"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0127FfF3m6sqs7YT6Ycq1CaC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  放弃psychometric measurement drift framing。Reframe为纯empirical characterization paper：\n  'Large-Scale Item-Level Stability Analysis of LLM Benchmarks'。MH statistic降级为nonparametric\n  group-comparison test，不依赖latent trait interpretation。Semi-synthetic framework成为anchor\n  contribution。Item-level stability定位为benchmark maintenance的operational metric。\n  Permutation null揭示temporal label assignment本身引入12-20%的spurious C%，31%中大量来自\n  cohort composition而非genuine item drift。RL robustness失败进一步削弱DIF作为stable detector\n  的叙事。8页内必须同时容纳reframing叙事和精简后的实验——需重构论文结构。\n  审稿人collective rejection预期：98% IRT misfit + unidimensional assumption on 57-subject\n  benchmark = 'MH-DIF results are uninterpretable without multidimensional IRT'。\n  Ground truth meta-critique被驳为straw man。Ability confound的2.4pp被认为低估。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      Apply MH-DIF to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508 items).\n      Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound\n      control, domain-specificity analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n      temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.322\n      temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n      ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n      ability_enrichment: 1.19\n      within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n      within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n      domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n      domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n      sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n      irt_misfit_pct_lz_gt2: 98.2\n      permutation_null_c_pct_posterior: 16.4\n      effective_c_pct_after_permutation_control: 14.9\n      domain_specificity_chi2_p: 0.78\n      negative_disc_items_sensitivity: \"removing 15.4% neg-disc items reduces C% by only 1.2pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      表面数字与registry一致（31.3% C%），但在worst档下，plan_029的permutation null将揭示\n      temporal label assignment本身产生~16.4%的spurious C%——即随机打乱2023/2024标签后，\n      仅因cohort composition差异（ability distribution shift d=-0.17, model family结构差异,\n      training data vintage差异）就能产生大量MH-DIF flags。这意味着31.3%中仅约14.9%\n      可归因于genuine item-level behavioral change。Within-family分析（Llama-2v3 C%=61.3%）\n      本应作为confound control，但在worst档下审稿人指出：Llama-2→3不是单纯temporal shift，\n      而是architecture+data+training全面重构，within-family DIF不能isolate contamination。\n      Domain specificity的ρ=0.307被审稿人dismisses为ecological correlation on N=57 subjects，\n      无item-level causal interpretation。98%的IRT misfit（|Lz|>2）在worst档下不再被接受为\n      \"reflects multidimensionality, discuss in limitations\"——审稿人要求multidimensional IRT\n      作为前提条件，否则MH-DIF结果uninterpretable。Enrichment≈1.0依然成立但被重新解读：\n      \"当然web-overlap和DIF不相关，这不是discovery而是trivially expected\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [metric, raw_value, after_permutation_control, reviewer_interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [C%, 31.3%, \"14.9% (31.3 - 16.4 null)\", \"inflated by cohort composition\"]\n          - [enrichment_vs_Li, 0.96, 0.96, \"trivially expected, not informative\"]\n          - [IRT_misfit, \"98% |Lz|>2\", N/A, \"renders MH conditioning unreliable\"]\n          - [domain_rho, 0.307, N/A, \"ecological fallacy on N=57\"]\n          - [within_family_C%, \"38.7-61.3%\", N/A, \"confounded by architecture change\"]\n      - title: \"Table 2: Cohort Definition × Item Filtering Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [cohort, filter, c_pct, effective_c_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [temporal, all_items, 31.3, 14.9]\n          - [temporal, no_neg_disc, 30.1, 13.7]\n          - [ability, all_items, 2.9, N/A]\n          - [ability, no_neg_disc, 2.7, N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Histogram of permutation null C% distribution (1000 permutations) with observed 31.3% marked. The null distribution centers at ~16.4% with SD~2.1%, making observed value only ~7σ above null mean — still significant, but the null is not near zero.\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter of subject-level C% vs domain accuracy improvement, showing ρ=0.307 but with massive residual variance — 5 subjects with >40% C% but near-zero accuracy improvement.\"\n    analysis: >\n      在worst档下，plan_001的核心结果从\"31% instability is genuine and robust\"变为\n      \"31% raw C%中约一半来自cohort composition artifacts\"。这不是statistical artifact\n      （random split仍为0.18%），而是temporal label本身proxy了多个未控制confound。\n      Reframing策略：不再claim \"31% items show genuine measurement drift\"，而是\n      \"we observe 31% item-level behavioral heterogeneity between temporal cohorts,\n      of which 10-18% persists after permutation controls — we characterize this\n      heterogeneity without claiming psychometric interpretation\"。\n\n  - name: rl_robustness_validation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      Validate DIF robustness to reasoning-RL models. Add 10-15 GRPO/PPO models to\n      focal cohort; measure DIF flag stability. Compare traditional detectors (Min-K%,\n      ConStat) on RL models individually.\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_temporal_c_pct: 31.3\n      with_alignment_rl_c_pct: 29.8\n      with_reasoning_rl_c_pct: 24.1\n      jaccard_baseline_vs_alignment_rl: 0.82\n      jaccard_baseline_vs_reasoning_rl: 0.43\n      jaccard_alignment_vs_reasoning_rl: 0.48\n      traditional_mink_auroc_base: 0.71\n      traditional_mink_auroc_rl: 0.68\n      traditional_constat_auroc_base: 0.65\n      traditional_constat_auroc_rl: 0.62\n      auroc_drop_mink: 0.03\n      auroc_drop_constat: 0.03\n      delong_p_mink: 0.34\n      delong_p_constat: 0.41\n      tost_equivalence_p: 0.08\n      n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n      power_analysis_delta_boundary: 1.8\n      bootstrap_ci_jaccard_rl: [0.31, 0.54]\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档下，reasoning-RL模型加入focal cohort后，DIF flags大幅shift（Jaccard=0.43,\n      远低于0.8的stability阈值）。原因：reasoning-RL模型（DeepSeek-R1, Qwen2.5-RL等）\n      的response pattern与标准decoder-only模型本质不同——它们在chain-of-thought后达到答案，\n      item difficulty profile完全改变。MH-DIF的ability conditioning基于total score，\n      但reasoning-RL模型的total score来源（deliberate reasoning vs memorization）与\n      传统模型不同，导致conditioning variable被confound。C%从31.3%降至24.1%——不是因为\n      RL模型\"更干净\"，而是因为cohort composition shift改变了哪些items被flag。\n      传统detectors的AUROC drop很小（0.03），审稿人据此argue：\"DIF对cohort composition\n      敏感而传统方法不敏感，说明DIF的sensitivity实际上是instability的体现\"。\n      TOST equivalence test borderline不通过（p=0.08），无法claim DIF和传统方法等效。\n      N=13 reasoning-RL模型本身就是underpowered的——worst档下这被视为fatal flaw，\n      不是\"supplementary\"而是\"insufficient to support any RL robustness claim\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: DIF Flag Stability Under Cohort Composition Changes\"\n        columns: [comparison, jaccard, c_pct_shift, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline vs +alignment-RL\", 0.82, \"-1.5pp\", \"stable (DPO/ORPO不影响)\"]\n          - [\"baseline vs +reasoning-RL\", 0.43, \"-7.2pp\", \"UNSTABLE — flags shift fundamentally\"]\n          - [\"alignment-RL vs reasoning-RL\", 0.48, \"-5.7pp\", \"RL type matters more than temporal split\"]\n      - title: \"Table 4: Traditional Detector AUROC Comparison\"\n        columns: [detector, auroc_base, auroc_rl, delta, delong_p]\n        rows:\n          - [Min-K%, 0.71, 0.68, -0.03, 0.34]\n          - [ConStat, 0.65, 0.62, -0.03, 0.41]\n          - [MH-DIF, N/A, N/A, \"Jaccard=0.43\", N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Venn diagram of DIF-C items across three cohort compositions (baseline, +alignment-RL, +reasoning-RL). Only 38% of items flagged in all three — DIF flags are cohort-dependent.\"\n      - \"Fig 4: Power curve for DIF detection as function of exploitation rate p, showing detection boundary shifts from δ=1.4 (baseline) to δ=1.8 (with RL models) — the zone of reliable detection shrinks.\"\n    analysis: >\n      RL robustness实验在worst档下彻底失败。Jaccard<0.55意味着DIF不能被视为cohort-invariant\n      detector。审稿人的解读：\"如果改变cohort中13个模型就导致43%的flag翻转，那DIF测量的\n      不是item property而是cohort property——这与psychometric DIF的理论前提矛盾\"。\n      Reframing下这变为：\"we acknowledge DIF flags are cohort-dependent — our characterization\n      is specific to the 2023-vs-2024 temporal split and should not be extrapolated to\n      arbitrary cohort definitions\"。这大幅削弱了generalizability claim。\n\n  - name: constat_perturbation_eval\n    plan_id: plan_003a\n    description: >\n      Independent evaluation of ConStat perturbation testing on MMLU: generate\n      reformulations for 200+ items, compare performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_reformulated: 237\n      constat_detection_rate_non_rl: 0.24\n      constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.09\n      constat_fpr: 0.06\n      constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.72\n      constat_auroc_rl: 0.54\n      reformulation_quality_score: 0.83\n      semantic_equivalence_verified: 0.91\n      fdr_threshold_q005: 0.048\n      constat_vs_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.15\n      constat_unique_detections: 47\n      dif_unique_detections: 312\n    result_rationale: >\n      ConStat在non-RL模型上表现合理（AUROC=0.72），在RL模型上大幅衰减（0.54，接近random）。\n      但在worst档下，关键问题不是ConStat表现如何，而是ConStat和DIF的detection overlap极低\n      （Jaccard=0.15）。审稿人解读：\"两个声称检测同一现象的方法几乎不flag同一批items，\n      说明它们测量的是不同东西——或者至少一个在测量artifact\"。ConStat的47个unique detections\n      中包含一些DIF完全miss的真实contamination cases（通过reformulation验证），\n      削弱了DIF作为primary detector的positioning。在reframed paper中，ConStat结果\n      降级为appendix baseline comparison，不再用于ensemble narrative（已dropped）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: ConStat Detection Performance\"\n        columns: [model_type, n_models, detection_rate, auroc, fpr]\n        rows:\n          - [non-RL, 50, 0.24, 0.72, 0.06]\n          - [alignment-RL, 30, 0.18, 0.64, 0.07]\n          - [reasoning-RL, 13, 0.09, 0.54, 0.05]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Overlap heatmap of DIF-C vs ConStat flags on the 237 reformulated items — near-zero correlation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      ConStat实验结果本身是informative的，但在worst档下strengthens审稿人argument：\n      item-level contamination detection整个领域缺乏construct validity——不同方法测量\n      不同东西，没有ground truth能判断谁对。这支持reframe到pure characterization paper。\n\n  - name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n    plan_id: plan_003b\n    description: >\n      Independent evaluation of DVD generation variance on MMLU: 50 responses per item\n      via temperature sampling on 10-15 models, detect bimodal distributions.\n    expected_results:\n      n_models_tested: 12\n      n_items_sampled: 500\n      responses_per_item: 50\n      temperature: 0.8\n      dvd_detection_rate: 0.18\n      dvd_auroc: 0.61\n      dvd_fpr: 0.08\n      bimodal_items_detected: 43\n      dvd_vs_dif_jaccard: 0.11\n      dvd_vs_constat_jaccard: 0.19\n      variant_contamination_coverage: 0.31\n      verbatim_contamination_coverage: 0.07\n      gpu_hours_used: 58\n    result_rationale: >\n      DVD在worst档下表现中等偏弱（AUROC=0.61）。Generation variance信号在LLM上比human\n      testing更noisy——temperature sampling的response分布本身就是multimodal的（model\n      confidence varies by item type, not just contamination）。DVD与DIF的overlap更低\n      （Jaccard=0.11），三个方法三个不同的item set。在worst档下，这个三方disagreement\n      成为审稿人最强的论据之一：\"when three independent detectors flag almost entirely\n      different items, the field has a construct validity crisis, not a contamination\n      detection toolbox\"。DVD的variant contamination coverage（0.31）比verbatim（0.07）\n      好得多，确认它确实测量不同phenomenon，但这恰恰支持meta-critique而非ensemble narrative。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: DVD Detection Summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [AUROC, 0.61]\n          - [detection_rate, 0.18]\n          - [FPR, 0.08]\n          - [bimodal_items, 43]\n          - [overlap_with_DIF (Jaccard), 0.11]\n          - [overlap_with_ConStat (Jaccard), 0.19]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Three-way Venn of DIF-C, ConStat, DVD flags — almost no items in triple-overlap zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      DVD结果在worst档下直接支持Claim 2的meta-critique（不同方法测量不同东西），\n      但ironically也削弱了paper自身的DIF-centric positioning。Reframed paper中，\n      DVD和ConStat结果用一段话提及作为\"multiple lenses on item heterogeneity\"的evidence，\n      不再pursuit ensemble fusion。\n\n  - name: ensemble_fusion\n    plan_id: plan_003c\n    description: >\n      Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble. Calibrate thresholds,\n      evaluate voting and weighted fusion, report coverage and precision.\n    expected_results:\n      ensemble_attempted: true\n      ensemble_viable: false\n      majority_vote_auroc: 0.58\n      weighted_fusion_auroc: 0.63\n      ensemble_fpr: 0.14\n      cross_val_weight_instability: \"weights flip sign across folds\"\n      uniform_weight_auroc: 0.60\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_dif_constat: 0.09\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_dif_dvd: 0.06\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_constat_dvd: 0.13\n      coverage_analysis: \"DIF covers 31%, ConStat 24%, DVD 18% — but only 4% in all three\"\n      decision: killed\n    result_rationale: >\n      Ensemble fusion在worst档下被kill。三个信号之间的correlation极低（0.06-0.13），\n      意味着它们不是measuring同一construct的noisy estimators，而是measuring不同constructs。\n      Majority vote AUROC（0.58）甚至低于单个最佳detector（ConStat 0.72 on non-RL），\n      因为vote要求agreement但signals几乎不agree。Weighted fusion cross-validation\n      显示权重在folds间高度不稳定（某些fold中DIF权重为负），表明没有stable fusion function。\n      FPR=0.14 borderline超过0.10 target。在worst档下，ensemble failure不是简单的\n      \"negative result\"——它是对整个contamination detection paradigm的existential challenge。\n      Paper中完全删除ensemble narrative，连appendix都不保留。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ensemble killed。在reframed paper中不提及。三方法disagreement作为meta-critique的\n      additional evidence在Discussion一句话提及。\n\n  - name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Replicate DIF analysis on GSM8K using GSM1K as ground truth. Temporal DIF,\n      semi-synthetic validation, GSM1K contamination gap correlation.\n    expected_results:\n      gsm8k_n_items: 1319\n      gsm8k_n_ref: 1017\n      gsm8k_n_foc: 804\n      gsm8k_temporal_c_pct: 12.4\n      gsm8k_external_c_pct: 38.1\n      gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n      gsm8k_permutation_null_c_pct: 8.7\n      gsm8k_effective_c_pct: 3.7\n      semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_standard_p10: 0.38\n      semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_external_p10: 0.27\n      gsm1k_correlation_n: 33\n      gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.29\n      gsm1k_pearson_p: 0.10\n      gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.22\n      gsm1k_spearman_p: 0.21\n      gsm1k_partial_r: -0.18\n      gsm1k_partial_p: 0.32\n      gsm1k_ci_upper: 0.06\n      direction: \"still negative but non-significant\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      GSM8K在worst档下表现远弱于MMLU。Temporal C%仅12.4%（worst档cross_benchmark_c_pct_min\n      范围8-14%），扣除permutation null（8.7%）后effective C%仅3.7%——接近noise floor。\n      原因：GSM8K是single-domain math benchmark，items之间homogeneity更高，temporal\n      cohort间的ability差异更直接映射到item difficulty（math能力提升→所有items变容易），\n      MH的ability conditioning更有效地absorb了这个effect。但也可能是GSM8K确实更stable。\n      Semi-synthetic ΔTPR显著降低（worst档0.25-0.4范围），因为smaller item pool（1319 vs 12508）\n      导致power降低，且single-domain matching variable更noisy。\n      GSM1K correlation从registry的-0.478(p=0.005)恶化到-0.29(p=0.10)——在worst档下\n      N=33太小，置信区间覆盖zero。审稿人判定：\"N=33 with CI crossing zero is not evidence\n      for anything\"。Direction仍为negative（与contamination hypothesis相反），\n      但在worst档下这被视为\"noise, not signal\"。GSM1K分析降级为appendix exploratory。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Cross-Benchmark DIF Comparison (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, raw_c_pct, permutation_null, effective_c_pct, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 31.3, 16.4, 14.9, \"moderate signal after controls\"]\n          - [GSM8K, 12.4, 8.7, 3.7, \"near noise floor\"]\n      - title: \"Table 8: GSM1K Correlation Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [metric, value, ci_95, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [Pearson r, -0.29, \"[-0.58, 0.06]\", 0.10]\n          - [Spearman ρ, -0.22, \"[-0.53, 0.14]\", 0.21]\n          - [Partial r, -0.18, \"[-0.50, 0.19]\", 0.32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: GSM8K permutation null distribution — observed 12.4% barely extends beyond the null range (8.7% mean, SD 1.4%), z=2.6.\"\n      - \"Fig 6: GSM1K scatter plot with wide CI bands crossing zero — visually unconvincing.\"\n    analysis: >\n      GSM8K结果在worst档下严重削弱cross-benchmark generalizability claim。Effective C%=3.7%\n      意味着GSM8K上几乎没有genuine item-level DIF。Reframed paper中，GSM8K从\"cross-benchmark\n      validation\"降级为\"the method produces different results on different benchmarks —\n      this heterogeneity itself is worth characterizing\"。GSM1K correlation完全dropped\n      from claims。\n\n  - name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      Pilot bifactor IRT equating on MMLU: fit bifactor model, select anchor items,\n      fixed-parameter calibration of replacements, demonstrate equated score equivalence.\n    expected_results:\n      bifactor_convergence: false\n      bifactor_attempts: 3\n      bifactor_rmsea: 0.089\n      bifactor_cfi: 0.72\n      bifactor_tli: 0.69\n      bifactor_srmr: 0.11\n      fallback_2pl_rmsea: 0.094\n      fallback_2pl_cfi: 0.68\n      anchor_item_selection_possible: false\n      equated_rho: null\n      decision: killed\n      reason: \"bifactor model fails to converge on 12508×5219 matrix; even when forced, fit indices far below acceptable thresholds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bifactor IRT在worst档下完全失败。12,508 items × 57 subjects的bifactor model\n      （1 general + 57 specific factors）有>25,000 parameters，在5,219 models上\n      severely overparameterized。Convergence failure after 3 attempts with different\n      starting values和estimation methods（MHRM, EM, QN）。即使forced convergence\n      的fit indices（RMSEA=0.089, CFI=0.72）远低于acceptable thresholds（RMSEA<0.06,\n      CFI>0.95）。这directly confirms审稿人的核心concern：\"unidimensional IRT assumption\n      severely violated, and bifactor doesn't rescue it because the item-to-model ratio\n      is too small for the factor structure\"。Anchor item selection不可能——没有reliable\n      parameter estimates。Equating pilot killed。在worst档下这是paper最致命的finding之一：\n      不仅unidimensional IRT不work，连multidimensional IRT也不work on this data。\n      Reframing response：完全放弃IRT-based interpretation，将MH当作nonparametric test。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: IRT Model Fit Comparison\"\n        columns: [model, rmsea, cfi, tli, srmr, converged]\n        rows:\n          - [unidimensional 2PL, 0.094, 0.68, 0.65, 0.12, \"yes (poor fit)\"]\n          - [bifactor (57 specific), 0.089, 0.72, 0.69, 0.11, \"no (forced)\"]\n          - [acceptable thresholds, \"<0.06\", \">0.95\", \">0.95\", \"<0.08\", N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Convergence trace showing parameter oscillation across 3000 EM iterations — no stable solution.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bifactor failure是worst档的defining event之一。它证实了审稿人的核心concern：\n      MMLU的57-subject structure使得any IRT model都是misspecified的。但在reframed paper中，\n      这反而成为strength：我们explicitly acknowledge IRT assumptions violated，\n      所以我们不依赖IRT interpretation——MH作为nonparametric χ² test不需要IRT model fit。\n      Bifactor结果在limitations section作为\"we attempted and it failed\"报告。\n\n  - name: item_generation_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation\n      with construct constraints. Calibrate via student simulation.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_generated: 200\n      n_items_quality_filtered: 142\n      difficulty_correlation_prompt_based: 0.18\n      difficulty_correlation_student_sim: 0.41\n      difficulty_correlation_target: 0.75\n      construct_alignment_score: 0.64\n      replacement_equating_rho: 0.88\n      replacement_equating_target: 0.95\n      student_sim_correlation_with_actual: 0.52\n      decision: killed_from_main_body\n    result_rationale: >\n      Item generation在worst档下表现远低于target。Prompt-based difficulty targeting\n      几乎无效（ρ=0.18，consistent with literature的0.10-0.45 range低端）。Student\n      simulation calibration有所改善（ρ=0.41）但远低于target 0.75——student simulation\n      on MMLU的multi-domain knowledge items比single-domain math items（arXiv报告的\n      r=0.75-0.82）困难得多。Generated items的construct alignment也不足（0.64），\n      因为MMLU items涵盖highly specialized domain knowledge，LLM generation的semantic\n      equivalence不保证psychometric equivalence。Equating rho=0.88低于0.95 target。\n      在worst档下，整个regeneration pipeline不可行。但这与reframing一致——\n      reframed paper不claim regeneration，而是characterization + toolkit for monitoring。\n      Item generation结果完全dropped，不进appendix（避免给审稿人攻击面）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Difficulty Calibration Methods Comparison\"\n        columns: [method, rho, target, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [prompt-based, 0.18, 0.75, FAIL]\n          - [student simulation, 0.41, 0.75, FAIL]\n          - [combined, 0.47, 0.75, FAIL]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter of target difficulty vs achieved difficulty — massive dispersion, especially for high-difficulty specialized items.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Item generation failure在worst档下是expected的——它依赖于IRT calibration\n      （plan_005已失败）和accurate difficulty prediction（both methods underperform）。\n      从paper中完全删除。\n\n  - name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Implement cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006). Simulate 4\n      successive administrations. Show cumulative power improvement.\n    expected_results:\n      n_simulated_administrations: 4\n      individual_admin_power: 0.40\n      cumulative_2_admin_power: 0.49\n      cumulative_3_admin_power: 0.56\n      cumulative_4_admin_power: 0.61\n      target_cumulative_3_power: 0.70\n      prior_specification_sensitivity: \"results vary 0.48-0.64 across 3 prior choices\"\n      simulation_n_per_admin: 200\n      delta_simulated: 1.0\n      decision: appendix_only\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cumulative Bayesian DIF在worst档下power improvement不达标。3次administration\n      后power仅0.56（target 0.70），4次仅0.61。原因：Sinharay et al.的方法假设successive\n      administrations的examinee populations来自same distribution（exchangeable），\n      但LLM benchmarks中successive cohorts的ability distribution系统性shift（新模型\n      systematically stronger）。Prior accumulation被ability drift corrupted——\n      previous administrations的DIF evidence可能来自ability confound而非genuine item change，\n      累积这些evidence amplifies bias而非reduces noise。Prior specification sensitivity\n      也高（0.48-0.64 range），意味着结果依赖于subjective prior choice。\n      在worst档下，这是simulation-only结果，没有real data validation，审稿人视为\n      underdeveloped。Reframed paper中作为appendix \"future direction\" sketch保留，\n      但不占main body任何空间。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Cumulative DIF Power by Administration Count\"\n        columns: [n_administrations, power, target, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.40, 0.70, -0.30]\n          - [2, 0.49, 0.70, -0.21]\n          - [3, 0.56, 0.70, -0.14]\n          - [4, 0.61, 0.70, -0.09]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Power accumulation curve with 95% CI bands — all below 0.70 target line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cumulative Bayesian DIF不达标，但不是blocking issue——reframed paper不依赖\n      longitudinal monitoring power。移至appendix作为future work motivation。\n\n  - name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement.\n      Simulate 5%-50% replacement, measure ranking stability and construct coverage.\n    expected_results:\n      replacement_5pct_rho: 0.998\n      replacement_10pct_rho: 0.994\n      replacement_20pct_rho: 0.981\n      replacement_50pct_rho: 0.937\n      construct_coverage_5pct: 0.97\n      construct_coverage_20pct: 0.88\n      construct_coverage_50pct: 0.71\n      reliability_alpha_original: 0.94\n      reliability_alpha_20pct_replaced: 0.86\n      reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.74\n      theoretical_bound_rho_at_31pct: 0.969\n      decision: appendix_supplementary\n    result_rationale: >\n      Graceful degradation分析在worst档下显示replacement不如预期robust。20% replacement\n      时rho=0.981尚可接受，但reliability从0.94降到0.86——接近educational testing的\n      minimum threshold（0.85）。50% replacement时reliability=0.74，clearly unacceptable。\n      Construct coverage也rapidly degrades——替换items无法maintain MMLU的57-subject\n      knowledge structure。这组结果在worst档下strengthens \"instability ≠ invalidity\"\n      narrative的另一面：removing unstable items 不是好的remediation strategy（at 31%,\n      reliability drops to ~0.85 boundary）。但它也意味着DIF-based benchmark maintenance\n      （audit protocol的\"act\" tier at C%>25）在operational上是risky的。\n      Reframed paper中，这个结果支持\"characterize, don't fix\"的message——\n      用一段话在Discussion中提及，详细数据移appendix。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Graceful Degradation Under Replacement\"\n        columns: [replacement_pct, ranking_rho, reliability_alpha, coverage]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.000, 0.94, 1.00]\n          - [5, 0.998, 0.93, 0.97]\n          - [10, 0.994, 0.91, 0.93]\n          - [20, 0.981, 0.86, 0.88]\n          - [31, 0.969, 0.85, 0.82]\n          - [50, 0.937, 0.74, 0.71]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Three-panel degradation curve (rho, alpha, coverage) vs replacement percentage — all show non-linear acceleration past 20%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果支持\"monitoring over remediation\"的operational message。在worst档下，\n      直接item removal/replacement不是viable strategy for 31% instability。\n      Reframed paper中作为operational guidance的evidence basis。\n\n  - name: item_focused_trees\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      Implement Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) as alternative to categorical\n      cohort DIF. Treat model release date as continuous covariate.\n    expected_results:\n      ift_implemented: true\n      ift_n_items_flagged: 2847\n      ift_dif_pct: 22.8\n      ift_vs_mh_jaccard: 0.52\n      ift_vs_mh_concordance: 0.71\n      ift_split_points_temporal: \"majority split at 2023-Q3 to 2024-Q1\"\n      ift_nonlinear_dif_detected: 312\n      ift_rmsea_improvement: null\n      ift_advantage: \"avoids arbitrary cohort splits\"\n      ift_disadvantage: \"tree instability — different random seeds yield different splits\"\n      tree_stability_jaccard_across_seeds: 0.63\n      decision: appendix_robustness_check\n    result_rationale: >\n      IFT在worst档下给出与MH partially concordant但不fully consistent的结果。\n      C%=22.8%（低于MH的31.3%），Jaccard=0.52——meaning approximately half the items\n      flagged by each method are unique to that method。IFT的优势（continuous covariate,\n      no arbitrary split）被tree instability抵消——across random seeds的Jaccard仅0.63，\n      意味着IFT结果本身不reproducible。IFT发现312个nonlinear DIF items（difficulty change\n      is non-monotonic over time），这是MH无法detect的，但在worst档下审稿人视为\n      \"additional evidence that the signal is noisy and method-dependent, not that\n      nonlinear DIF is a real phenomenon\"。IFT的split points集中在2023-Q3到2024-Q1，\n      与temporal cohort split大致对齐——这验证了temporal split的合理性，但也意味着\n      IFT没有提供fundamentally new information。在reframed paper中作为appendix\n      robustness check保留，main body一句话提及\"results qualitatively consistent\n      with continuous-covariate alternative\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\"\n        columns: [method, c_pct, unique_flags, overlap_jaccard]\n        rows:\n          - [MH-DIF, 31.3, 1583, 0.52]\n          - [IFT, 22.8, 512, 0.52]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Example Item-Focused Tree showing temporal split at 2023-Q4 — qualitatively consistent with binary cohort split.\"\n    analysis: >\n      IFT结果在worst档下是double-edged：支持temporal split的合理性，但method disagreement\n      （Jaccard=0.52）加入审稿人的\"method-dependent results\"narrative。Appendix only。\n\n  - name: architecture_stratified_dif\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      Run DIF within architecture-homogeneous decoder-only subpopulation. Report IRT\n      fit diagnostics. Compare C% and detection power vs full population.\n    expected_results:\n      n_decoder_only: 5226\n      n_non_decoder: 1\n      pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n      decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n      decoder_only_jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n      irt_rmsea_full: 0.094\n      irt_rmsea_decoder_only: 0.094\n      irt_cfi_full: 0.68\n      irt_cfi_decoder_only: 0.68\n      fit_improvement: \"none — removing 1 model changes nothing\"\n      conclusion: \"architecture heterogeneity is not the source of IRT misfit\"\n      real_source_of_misfit: \"57-subject multidimensionality + non-normal ability distribution\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Architecture stratification在worst档下确认了一个重要但trivial的finding：\n      METABENCH MMLU是99.98% decoder-only（5226/5227），removing 1个non-decoder model\n      changes absolutely nothing。C%不变（31.3%），Jaccard=1.0，IRT fit不变。\n      这experiment本身是correct（排除architecture heterogeneity作为concern），\n      但在worst档下审稿人说：\"我们从未argue architecture heterogeneity是问题——问题是\n      57-subject multidimensionality + 非正态ability distribution + model non-independence。\n      你们排除了一个straw man concern\"。IRT fit仍然terrible（RMSEA=0.094, CFI=0.68），\n      因为真正的misfit来源（multidimensionality）没有被addressed。\n      在reframed paper中，architecture homogeneity作为一句话fact（\"METABENCH MMLU is\n      99.98% decoder-only\"）报告，不需要单独实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Architecture Stratification (Moot)\"\n        columns: [population, n_models, c_pct, rmsea, cfi]\n        rows:\n          - [full, 5227, 31.3, 0.094, 0.68]\n          - [decoder-only, 5226, 31.3, 0.094, 0.68]\n          - [delta, 1, 0.0, 0.000, 0.00]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      实验本身结论正确（architecture不是问题），但在worst档下被视为wasted space。\n      Reframed paper中压缩为半句话。\n\n  - name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      Inject known contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure DIF\n      detection power under controlled ground truth. Vary injection parameters.\n    expected_results:\n      n_clean_items_selected: 500\n      n_injected_items: 150\n      temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.39\n      temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.58\n      temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.74\n      temporal_external_tpr_p10: 0.87\n      temporal_external_fpr: 0.318\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p03: 0.07\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.26\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p07: 0.42\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.55\n      ability_external_tpr_p10: 0.62\n      ability_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.19\n      fpr_inflation_at_p10_standard: 0.298_to_0.58\n      matching_variable_contamination: true\n      cross_subject_matching_delta_fpr: 0.003\n      replication_delta_tpr_range: \"[0.25, 0.40]\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Semi-synthetic在worst档下ΔTPR显著低于registry记录。P=0.5时ΔTPR=0.26（registry为\n      0.508），p=1.0时ΔTPR=0.55（registry为0.674）。差异来源：worst档下的injection\n      使用更conservative的parameter choices——injected items选自difficulty分布中间段\n      （避免easy items的ceiling effect），focal group size更接近minimum（N≈100 vs\n      registry的N=807），exploitation rate的effective signal更小（因为\"clean\" baseline\n      items本身已有31%被flag为C-class，diluting the injection signal）。\n      关键问题：baseline FPR=0.318意味着没有injection时就有31.8%的items被flag——\n      ΔTPR必须在这个high baseline上demonstrate增量，signal-to-noise ratio差。\n      Cross-subject matching仍然有效（ΔFPR≈0.003，接近zero），这是anchor finding。\n      但ΔTPR的magnitude（worst档0.25-0.40）审稿人判定为\"moderate at best —\n      the framework works but detection power is underwhelming\"。\n      在reframed paper中，semi-synthetic framework仍是anchor contribution——\n      但framing从\"powerful detection tool\"变为\"principled validation infrastructure\n      with known power limitations\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 15: Semi-Synthetic ΔTPR Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [injection_p, tpr, baseline_fpr, delta_tpr, registry_delta_tpr]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 0.39, 0.318, 0.07, 0.222]\n          - [0.5, 0.58, 0.318, 0.26, 0.508]\n          - [0.7, 0.74, 0.318, 0.42, 0.664]\n          - [1.0, 0.87, 0.318, 0.55, 0.674]\n      - title: \"Table 16: Cross-Subject vs Within-Subject Matching\"\n        columns: [matching, delta_fpr, delta_tpr_p05, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [within-subject, \"+0.186\", 0.34, \"FPR inflation — contaminated matching var\"]\n          - [cross-subject, \"+0.003\", 0.26, \"FPR stable — anchor finding preserved\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Dose-response curve (injection p vs ΔTPR) — monotonic but flatter than registry, reaching 0.55 at p=1.0.\"\n      - \"Fig 9: FPR stability comparison — cross-subject matching maintains ΔFPR≈0 across all injection levels.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic framework在worst档下power减弱但core innovation（cross-subject matching,\n      ΔFPR≈0）preserved。这成为reframed paper的anchor contribution——framework本身\n      不依赖IRT assumptions，是portable的method contribution。Power limitations\n      honestly reported。\n\n  - name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n    plan_id: plan_028\n    description: >\n      Run temporal DIF on additional benchmarks from METABENCH (ARC, HellaSwag,\n      WinoGrande, TruthfulQA, MMLU-Pro). Address \"only MMLU\" concern.\n    expected_results:\n      mmlu_c_pct: 31.3\n      mmlu_permutation_null: 16.4\n      mmlu_effective: 14.9\n      arc_c_pct: 13.8\n      arc_permutation_null: 9.2\n      arc_effective: 4.6\n      hellaswag_c_pct: 10.1\n      hellaswag_permutation_null: 7.8\n      hellaswag_effective: 2.3\n      winogrande_c_pct: 14.7\n      winogrande_permutation_null: 10.1\n      winogrande_effective: 4.6\n      truthfulqa_c_pct: 22.4\n      truthfulqa_permutation_null: 14.8\n      truthfulqa_effective: 7.6\n      gsm8k_c_pct: 12.4\n      gsm8k_permutation_null: 8.7\n      gsm8k_effective: 3.7\n      cross_benchmark_raw_range: \"10.1-31.3%\"\n      cross_benchmark_effective_range: \"2.3-14.9%\"\n      all_random_controls_below_1pct: true\n      mmlu_pro_not_available: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Multi-benchmark分析在worst档下揭示一个devastating pattern：raw C%在所有benchmarks\n      上都>10%（range 10.1-31.3%），但permutation null也consistently高（7.8-16.4%），\n      扣除后effective C%范围仅2.3-14.9%。MMLU的effective C%最高（14.9%）因为它有最多subjects\n      （57）和最大item pool（12508），提供更多opportunities for heterogeneity。\n      HellaSwag effective C%最低（2.3%），因为it's a relatively homogeneous task\n      （sentence completion）——item-level behavioral heterogeneity genuinely lower。\n      Cross-benchmark heterogeneity本身是informative的（\"different benchmarks have\n      different stability profiles\"），但审稿人concern是：\"if after permutation controls\n      some benchmarks show <5% effective C%, your '31% instability' headline is MMLU-specific\n      and cannot be generalized\"。在worst档下，\"31%\"的headline number必须qualified\n      with \"before permutation controls; effective rate 10-18% depending on benchmark\"。\n      Reframed paper中，cross-benchmark heterogeneity成为characterization的一部分：\n      \"benchmark stability varies from 2% (HellaSwag) to 15% (MMLU) — we provide\n      benchmark-specific profiles\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 17: Multi-Benchmark DIF Summary (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, n_items, raw_c_pct, permutation_null, effective_c_pct, random_control]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 12508, 31.3, 16.4, 14.9, 0.18]\n          - [TruthfulQA, 817, 22.4, 14.8, 7.6, 0.37]\n          - [WinoGrande, 1267, 14.7, 10.1, 4.6, 0.32]\n          - [ARC, 1172, 13.8, 9.2, 4.6, 0.60]\n          - [GSM8K, 1319, 12.4, 8.7, 3.7, 0.30]\n          - [HellaSwag, 10042, 10.1, 7.8, 2.3, 0.28]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Stacked bar chart: raw C% decomposed into permutation-null component and effective component per benchmark. MMLU dominates; HellaSwag nearly all null.\"\n      - \"Fig 11: Effective C% vs benchmark dimensionality (number of subtopics/categories) — positive correlation, suggesting multi-domain benchmarks show more item heterogeneity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-benchmark结果在worst档下是mixed news。好消息：all benchmarks show above-chance\n      DIF（random controls <1%）。坏消息：effective signal after permutation controls\n      很小for most benchmarks。Reframed paper必须honest about这个range。\n\n  - name: permutation_null_c_rate\n    plan_id: plan_029\n    description: >\n      1000× permutation test: randomly reassign 2023/2024 temporal labels, run MH-DIF\n      each time. Establish null distribution for C%.\n    expected_results:\n      n_permutations: 1000\n      null_c_pct_mean: 16.4\n      null_c_pct_sd: 2.1\n      null_c_pct_95ci: [12.6, 20.3]\n      null_c_pct_min: 10.8\n      null_c_pct_max: 22.7\n      observed_c_pct: 31.3\n      z_score: 7.1\n      p_value: \"<1e-12\"\n      effective_c_pct: 14.9\n      fraction_spurious: 0.524\n      null_mechanism: \"cohort composition differences (ability, family structure, training vintage) generate substantial DIF even without temporal signal\"\n      random_split_within_cohort_c_pct: 0.18\n      permutation_vs_random_split_gap: \"16.4 vs 0.18 — temporal label permutation preserves between-cohort structure\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Permutation null是worst档的defining experiment。1000次permutation（保持group sizes\n      N_ref=1080, N_foc=807不变，但随机打乱temporal labels）产生mean C%=16.4%（SD=2.1%），\n      95% range [12.6, 20.3]。这意味着即使temporal labels是random的，仅因为两组models\n      的composition差异（ability distribution overlap=76.4%, 不同model families的比例差异,\n      不同training data vintages的representation差异），MH-DIF就会flag 12-20%的items。\n      \n      关键区分：这不是与random-split control（0.18%）矛盾。Random split是within-cohort的\n      （same time period, same family composition），而permutation null是between-cohort的\n      （preserves the actual model composition, just shuffles temporal labels）。\n      The 16.4% null arises because models from 2023 and 2024 genuinely differ in ways\n      beyond temporal signal — model families, training approaches, scale distributions\n      all differ between cohorts. MH's ability conditioning (total score) cannot absorb\n      all these confounds.\n      \n      Observed 31.3% is still z=7.1 above null（p<1e-12），so temporal signal EXISTS\n      beyond cohort composition. But 52.4% of the raw C% is attributable to cohort\n      composition effects, not temporal item-level change. Effective C%=14.9%。\n      \n      在worst档下，审稿人的reaction：\n      \"这证实了我们的concern——31%中一半以上是cohort composition artifact。MH-DIF\n      在LLM context下的conditioning is fundamentally insufficient。14.9%可能也包含\n      未被permutation null capture的confounds（tokenizer changes, training data composition\n      within families）。The genuine temporal item-level signal may be even smaller。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 18: Permutation Null Distribution\"\n        columns: [statistic, value]\n        rows:\n          - [null_mean_c_pct, 16.4]\n          - [null_sd, 2.1]\n          - [null_95_ci, \"[12.6, 20.3]\"]\n          - [observed_c_pct, 31.3]\n          - [z_score, 7.1]\n          - [effective_c_pct, 14.9]\n          - [fraction_spurious, \"52.4%\"]\n          - [random_split_c_pct, 0.18]\n      - title: \"Table 19: Decomposition of Observed C%\"\n        columns: [source, contribution_pct, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [genuine_temporal_signal, 14.9, \"item-level behavioral change across model generations\"]\n          - [cohort_composition, 16.4, \"ability distribution + family structure + training vintage differences\"]\n          - [total, 31.3, N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: Histogram of 1000 permutation null C% values with observed 31.3% marked. Null distribution is NOT centered at zero — it's centered at 16.4%, far above the random-split baseline of 0.18%.\"\n      - \"Fig 13: Q-Q plot showing null distribution is approximately normal (Shapiro-Wilk p=0.34), validating z-test interpretation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Permutation null是worst档论文的central finding。它将31%的headline number decompose为\n      ~15% genuine + ~16% spurious。Reframed paper必须lead with这个decomposition：\n      \"we observe 31% raw behavioral heterogeneity, of which approximately half persists\n      after permutation controls — the remainder reflects cohort composition differences\n      that MH-DIF's total-score conditioning cannot absorb\"。这honest framing比\n      原来的\"31% instability\"更defensible，但也更modest。\n\n  - name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n    plan_id: plan_030\n    description: >\n      Supplement pseudo R² with odds ratio, CI, McFadden/Nagelkerke R², deviance ratio.\n      Add item-level accuracy change as predictor.\n    expected_results:\n      model1_domain_delta:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n        or_per_010: 1.55\n        or_ci: [1.19, 2.03]\n      model2_domain_plus_items:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.072\n        or_domain_per_010: 0.73\n        or_difficulty_per_010: 0.78\n        or_discrimination_per_010: 1.51\n      model3_item_delta:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0021\n        or_item_change_per_010: 1.08\n        or_item_ci: [1.51, 2.96]\n      model4_full:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0737\n        or_item_change_per_010: 0.92\n        or_difficulty_per_010: 0.77\n        or_discrimination_per_010: 1.54\n      simpsons_paradox: true\n      simpsons_direction: \"item accuracy change OR flips from 1.08 to 0.92 when controlling for item properties\"\n      deviance_explained_by_item_props: \"96% of model variance from difficulty + discrimination, not accuracy change\"\n      lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 647\n      lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 656\n    result_rationale: >\n      Odds ratio regression在worst档下confirms并extends原有findings。Domain-level\n      accuracy change（Model 1）是significant但tiny predictor（R²=0.0007）。Item-level\n      accuracy change（Model 3）marginally better（R²=0.0012）但still near zero。\n      Simpson's paradox preserved：item accuracy change OR从1.08降到0.92 when controlling\n      for item properties——meaning higher-accuracy-change items are actually LESS likely\n      to be DIF after controlling for difficulty and discrimination。\n      \n      在worst档下，审稿人的worst-case解读：\"item difficulty和discrimination explains 7%\n      of DIF variance（Model 4 R²=0.0737）。这虽然不高in absolute terms，但比accuracy\n      change高50倍。DIF flags与item properties相关——harder, more discriminating items\n      更likely被flag。这可能是MH statistic的statistical property（高discrimination items\n      产生更大的α_MH estimates），而非genuine item-level behavioral change\"。\n      \n      Plan_027的d=-0.17被审稿人认为是marginal的ability gap，但temporal label可能proxy\n      其他未控制confound（training data composition, tokenizer changes, RLHF procedures）。\n      这些confounds不会被total score matching absorb。\n      \n      在reframed paper中，regression transparency section支持honest framing：\"DIF flags\n      are weakly predicted by accuracy change but moderately predicted by item properties —\n      we report this transparently as part of our characterization\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 20: Logistic Regression Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [model, predictors, mcfadden_r2, nagelkerke_r2, key_or]\n        rows:\n          - [M1, domain_Δacc, 0.0007, 0.0012, \"1.55 [1.19-2.03]\"]\n          - [M2, domain_Δacc + item_props, 0.0423, 0.072, \"0.73 (Δacc flips)\"]\n          - [M3, item_Δacc, 0.0012, 0.0021, \"1.08\"]\n          - [M4, item_Δacc + item_props, 0.0434, 0.0737, \"0.92 (Δacc flips)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 14: Simpson's paradox visualization — marginal OR for accuracy change is >1 (DIF-promoting), but conditional OR is <1 (DIF-protective) after item property control.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Regression transparency strengthens honest framing但也gives审稿人ammunition：\n      \"item properties explain 50× more variance than accuracy change — DIF may be\n      a statistical artifact of item difficulty/discrimination structure\"。\n      Reframed paper must address this directly。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24168,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24168},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03381ec8-53c9-4c55-86f7-a45910704277","uuid":"7ad7cd7d-a79e-49d0-a138-f4020d650b89"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":377932,"duration_api_ms":379237,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  放弃psychometric measurement drift framing。Reframe为纯empirical characterization paper：\n  'Large-Scale Item-Level Stability Analysis of LLM Benchmarks'。MH statistic降级为nonparametric\n  group-comparison test，不依赖latent trait interpretation。Semi-synthetic framework成为anchor\n  contribution。Item-level stability定位为benchmark maintenance的operational metric。\n  Permutation null揭示temporal label assignment本身引入12-20%的spurious C%，31%中大量来自\n  cohort composition而非genuine item drift。RL robustness失败进一步削弱DIF作为stable detector\n  的叙事。8页内必须同时容纳reframing叙事和精简后的实验——需重构论文结构。\n  审稿人collective rejection预期：98% IRT misfit + unidimensional assumption on 57-subject\n  benchmark = 'MH-DIF results are uninterpretable without multidimensional IRT'。\n  Ground truth meta-critique被驳为straw man。Ability confound的2.4pp被认为低估。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: real_data_dif_mmlu\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      Apply MH-DIF to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,219 models × 12,508 items).\n      Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound\n      control, domain-specificity analysis.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n      temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.322\n      temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n      ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n      ability_enrichment: 1.19\n      within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n      within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct: 38.7\n      domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n      domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n      sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n      irt_misfit_pct_lz_gt2: 98.2\n      permutation_null_c_pct_posterior: 16.4\n      effective_c_pct_after_permutation_control: 14.9\n      domain_specificity_chi2_p: 0.78\n      negative_disc_items_sensitivity: \"removing 15.4% neg-disc items reduces C% by only 1.2pp\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      表面数字与registry一致（31.3% C%），但在worst档下，plan_029的permutation null将揭示\n      temporal label assignment本身产生~16.4%的spurious C%——即随机打乱2023/2024标签后，\n      仅因cohort composition差异（ability distribution shift d=-0.17, model family结构差异,\n      training data vintage差异）就能产生大量MH-DIF flags。这意味着31.3%中仅约14.9%\n      可归因于genuine item-level behavioral change。Within-family分析（Llama-2v3 C%=61.3%）\n      本应作为confound control，但在worst档下审稿人指出：Llama-2→3不是单纯temporal shift，\n      而是architecture+data+training全面重构，within-family DIF不能isolate contamination。\n      Domain specificity的ρ=0.307被审稿人dismisses为ecological correlation on N=57 subjects，\n      无item-level causal interpretation。98%的IRT misfit（|Lz|>2）在worst档下不再被接受为\n      \"reflects multidimensionality, discuss in limitations\"——审稿人要求multidimensional IRT\n      作为前提条件，否则MH-DIF结果uninterpretable。Enrichment≈1.0依然成立但被重新解读：\n      \"当然web-overlap和DIF不相关，这不是discovery而是trivially expected\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary (Worst-Tier Interpretation)\"\n        columns: [metric, raw_value, after_permutation_control, reviewer_interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [C%, 31.3%, \"14.9% (31.3 - 16.4 null)\", \"inflated by cohort composition\"]\n          - [enrichment_vs_Li, 0.96, 0.96, \"trivially expected, not informative\"]\n          - [IRT_misfit, \"98% |Lz|>2\", N/A, \"renders MH conditioning unreliable\"]\n          - [domain_rho, 0.307, N/A, \"ecological fallacy on N=57\"]\n          - [within_family_C%, \"38.7-61.3%\", N/A, \"confounded by architecture change\"]\n      - title: \"Table 2: Cohort Definition × Item Filtering Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [cohort, filter, c_pct, effective_c_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [temporal, all_items, 31.3, 14.9]\n          - [temporal, no_neg_disc, 30.1, 13.7]\n          - [ability, all_items, 2.9, N/A]\n          - [ability, no_neg_disc, 2.7, N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Histogram of permutation null C% distribution (1000 permutations) with observed 31.3% marked. The null distribution centers at ~16.4% with SD~2.1%, making observed value only ~7σ above null mean — still significant, but the null is not near zero.\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter of subject-level C% vs domain accuracy improvement, showing ρ=0.307 but with massive residual variance — 5 subjects with >40% C% but near-zero accuracy improvement.\"\n    analysis: >\n      在worst档下，plan_001的核心结果从\"31% instability is genuine and robust\"变为\n      \"31% raw C%中约一半来自cohort composition artifacts\"。这不是statistical artifact\n      （random split仍为0.18%），而是temporal label本身proxy了多个未控制confound。\n      Reframing策略：不再claim \"31% items show genuine measurement drift\"，而是\n      \"we observe 31% item-level behavioral heterogeneity between temporal cohorts,\n      of which 10-18% persists after permutation controls — we characterize this\n      heterogeneity without claiming psychometric interpretation\"。\n\n  - name: rl_robustness_validation\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      Validate DIF robustness to reasoning-RL models. Add 10-15 GRPO/PPO models to\n      focal cohort; measure DIF flag stability. Compare traditional detectors (Min-K%,\n      ConStat) on RL models individually.\n    expected_results:\n      baseline_temporal_c_pct: 31.3\n      with_alignment_rl_c_pct: 29.8\n      with_reasoning_rl_c_pct: 24.1\n      jaccard_baseline_vs_alignment_rl: 0.82\n      jaccard_baseline_vs_reasoning_rl: 0.43\n      jaccard_alignment_vs_reasoning_rl: 0.48\n      traditional_mink_auroc_base: 0.71\n      traditional_mink_auroc_rl: 0.68\n      traditional_constat_auroc_base: 0.65\n      traditional_constat_auroc_rl: 0.62\n      auroc_drop_mink: 0.03\n      auroc_drop_constat: 0.03\n      delong_p_mink: 0.34\n      delong_p_constat: 0.41\n      tost_equivalence_p: 0.08\n      n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n      power_analysis_delta_boundary: 1.8\n      bootstrap_ci_jaccard_rl: [0.31, 0.54]\n    result_rationale: >\n      在worst档下，reasoning-RL模型加入focal cohort后，DIF flags大幅shift（Jaccard=0.43,\n      远低于0.8的stability阈值）。原因：reasoning-RL模型（DeepSeek-R1, Qwen2.5-RL等）\n      的response pattern与标准decoder-only模型本质不同——它们在chain-of-thought后达到答案，\n      item difficulty profile完全改变。MH-DIF的ability conditioning基于total score，\n      但reasoning-RL模型的total score来源（deliberate reasoning vs memorization）与\n      传统模型不同，导致conditioning variable被confound。C%从31.3%降至24.1%——不是因为\n      RL模型\"更干净\"，而是因为cohort composition shift改变了哪些items被flag。\n      传统detectors的AUROC drop很小（0.03），审稿人据此argue：\"DIF对cohort composition\n      敏感而传统方法不敏感，说明DIF的sensitivity实际上是instability的体现\"。\n      TOST equivalence test borderline不通过（p=0.08），无法claim DIF和传统方法等效。\n      N=13 reasoning-RL模型本身就是underpowered的——worst档下这被视为fatal flaw，\n      不是\"supplementary\"而是\"insufficient to support any RL robustness claim\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 3: DIF Flag Stability Under Cohort Composition Changes\"\n        columns: [comparison, jaccard, c_pct_shift, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline vs +alignment-RL\", 0.82, \"-1.5pp\", \"stable (DPO/ORPO不影响)\"]\n          - [\"baseline vs +reasoning-RL\", 0.43, \"-7.2pp\", \"UNSTABLE — flags shift fundamentally\"]\n          - [\"alignment-RL vs reasoning-RL\", 0.48, \"-5.7pp\", \"RL type matters more than temporal split\"]\n      - title: \"Table 4: Traditional Detector AUROC Comparison\"\n        columns: [detector, auroc_base, auroc_rl, delta, delong_p]\n        rows:\n          - [Min-K%, 0.71, 0.68, -0.03, 0.34]\n          - [ConStat, 0.65, 0.62, -0.03, 0.41]\n          - [MH-DIF, N/A, N/A, \"Jaccard=0.43\", N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Venn diagram of DIF-C items across three cohort compositions (baseline, +alignment-RL, +reasoning-RL). Only 38% of items flagged in all three — DIF flags are cohort-dependent.\"\n      - \"Fig 4: Power curve for DIF detection as function of exploitation rate p, showing detection boundary shifts from δ=1.4 (baseline) to δ=1.8 (with RL models) — the zone of reliable detection shrinks.\"\n    analysis: >\n      RL robustness实验在worst档下彻底失败。Jaccard<0.55意味着DIF不能被视为cohort-invariant\n      detector。审稿人的解读：\"如果改变cohort中13个模型就导致43%的flag翻转，那DIF测量的\n      不是item property而是cohort property——这与psychometric DIF的理论前提矛盾\"。\n      Reframing下这变为：\"we acknowledge DIF flags are cohort-dependent — our characterization\n      is specific to the 2023-vs-2024 temporal split and should not be extrapolated to\n      arbitrary cohort definitions\"。这大幅削弱了generalizability claim。\n\n  - name: constat_perturbation_eval\n    plan_id: plan_003a\n    description: >\n      Independent evaluation of ConStat perturbation testing on MMLU: generate\n      reformulations for 200+ items, compare performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_reformulated: 237\n      constat_detection_rate_non_rl: 0.24\n      constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.09\n      constat_fpr: 0.06\n      constat_auroc_non_rl: 0.72\n      constat_auroc_rl: 0.54\n      reformulation_quality_score: 0.83\n      semantic_equivalence_verified: 0.91\n      fdr_threshold_q005: 0.048\n      constat_vs_dif_overlap_jaccard: 0.15\n      constat_unique_detections: 47\n      dif_unique_detections: 312\n    result_rationale: >\n      ConStat在non-RL模型上表现合理（AUROC=0.72），在RL模型上大幅衰减（0.54，接近random）。\n      但在worst档下，关键问题不是ConStat表现如何，而是ConStat和DIF的detection overlap极低\n      （Jaccard=0.15）。审稿人解读：\"两个声称检测同一现象的方法几乎不flag同一批items，\n      说明它们测量的是不同东西——或者至少一个在测量artifact\"。ConStat的47个unique detections\n      中包含一些DIF完全miss的真实contamination cases（通过reformulation验证），\n      削弱了DIF作为primary detector的positioning。在reframed paper中，ConStat结果\n      降级为appendix baseline comparison，不再用于ensemble narrative（已dropped）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 5: ConStat Detection Performance\"\n        columns: [model_type, n_models, detection_rate, auroc, fpr]\n        rows:\n          - [non-RL, 50, 0.24, 0.72, 0.06]\n          - [alignment-RL, 30, 0.18, 0.64, 0.07]\n          - [reasoning-RL, 13, 0.09, 0.54, 0.05]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Overlap heatmap of DIF-C vs ConStat flags on the 237 reformulated items — near-zero correlation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      ConStat实验结果本身是informative的，但在worst档下strengthens审稿人argument：\n      item-level contamination detection整个领域缺乏construct validity——不同方法测量\n      不同东西，没有ground truth能判断谁对。这支持reframe到pure characterization paper。\n\n  - name: dvd_generation_variance_eval\n    plan_id: plan_003b\n    description: >\n      Independent evaluation of DVD generation variance on MMLU: 50 responses per item\n      via temperature sampling on 10-15 models, detect bimodal distributions.\n    expected_results:\n      n_models_tested: 12\n      n_items_sampled: 500\n      responses_per_item: 50\n      temperature: 0.8\n      dvd_detection_rate: 0.18\n      dvd_auroc: 0.61\n      dvd_fpr: 0.08\n      bimodal_items_detected: 43\n      dvd_vs_dif_jaccard: 0.11\n      dvd_vs_constat_jaccard: 0.19\n      variant_contamination_coverage: 0.31\n      verbatim_contamination_coverage: 0.07\n      gpu_hours_used: 58\n    result_rationale: >\n      DVD在worst档下表现中等偏弱（AUROC=0.61）。Generation variance信号在LLM上比human\n      testing更noisy——temperature sampling的response分布本身就是multimodal的（model\n      confidence varies by item type, not just contamination）。DVD与DIF的overlap更低\n      （Jaccard=0.11），三个方法三个不同的item set。在worst档下，这个三方disagreement\n      成为审稿人最强的论据之一：\"when three independent detectors flag almost entirely\n      different items, the field has a construct validity crisis, not a contamination\n      detection toolbox\"。DVD的variant contamination coverage（0.31）比verbatim（0.07）\n      好得多，确认它确实测量不同phenomenon，但这恰恰支持meta-critique而非ensemble narrative。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 6: DVD Detection Summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [AUROC, 0.61]\n          - [detection_rate, 0.18]\n          - [FPR, 0.08]\n          - [bimodal_items, 43]\n          - [overlap_with_DIF (Jaccard), 0.11]\n          - [overlap_with_ConStat (Jaccard), 0.19]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Three-way Venn of DIF-C, ConStat, DVD flags — almost no items in triple-overlap zone.\"\n    analysis: >\n      DVD结果在worst档下直接支持Claim 2的meta-critique（不同方法测量不同东西），\n      但ironically也削弱了paper自身的DIF-centric positioning。Reframed paper中，\n      DVD和ConStat结果用一段话提及作为\"multiple lenses on item heterogeneity\"的evidence，\n      不再pursuit ensemble fusion。\n\n  - name: ensemble_fusion\n    plan_id: plan_003c\n    description: >\n      Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble. Calibrate thresholds,\n      evaluate voting and weighted fusion, report coverage and precision.\n    expected_results:\n      ensemble_attempted: true\n      ensemble_viable: false\n      majority_vote_auroc: 0.58\n      weighted_fusion_auroc: 0.63\n      ensemble_fpr: 0.14\n      cross_val_weight_instability: \"weights flip sign across folds\"\n      uniform_weight_auroc: 0.60\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_dif_constat: 0.09\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_dif_dvd: 0.06\n      pairwise_signal_correlation_constat_dvd: 0.13\n      coverage_analysis: \"DIF covers 31%, ConStat 24%, DVD 18% — but only 4% in all three\"\n      decision: killed\n    result_rationale: >\n      Ensemble fusion在worst档下被kill。三个信号之间的correlation极低（0.06-0.13），\n      意味着它们不是measuring同一construct的noisy estimators，而是measuring不同constructs。\n      Majority vote AUROC（0.58）甚至低于单个最佳detector（ConStat 0.72 on non-RL），\n      因为vote要求agreement但signals几乎不agree。Weighted fusion cross-validation\n      显示权重在folds间高度不稳定（某些fold中DIF权重为负），表明没有stable fusion function。\n      FPR=0.14 borderline超过0.10 target。在worst档下，ensemble failure不是简单的\n      \"negative result\"——它是对整个contamination detection paradigm的existential challenge。\n      Paper中完全删除ensemble narrative，连appendix都不保留。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Ensemble killed。在reframed paper中不提及。三方法disagreement作为meta-critique的\n      additional evidence在Discussion一句话提及。\n\n  - name: cross_benchmark_gsm8k\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      Replicate DIF analysis on GSM8K using GSM1K as ground truth. Temporal DIF,\n      semi-synthetic validation, GSM1K contamination gap correlation.\n    expected_results:\n      gsm8k_n_items: 1319\n      gsm8k_n_ref: 1017\n      gsm8k_n_foc: 804\n      gsm8k_temporal_c_pct: 12.4\n      gsm8k_external_c_pct: 38.1\n      gsm8k_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n      gsm8k_permutation_null_c_pct: 8.7\n      gsm8k_effective_c_pct: 3.7\n      semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_standard_p10: 0.38\n      semi_synthetic_delta_tpr_external_p10: 0.27\n      gsm1k_correlation_n: 33\n      gsm1k_pearson_r: -0.29\n      gsm1k_pearson_p: 0.10\n      gsm1k_spearman_rho: -0.22\n      gsm1k_spearman_p: 0.21\n      gsm1k_partial_r: -0.18\n      gsm1k_partial_p: 0.32\n      gsm1k_ci_upper: 0.06\n      direction: \"still negative but non-significant\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      GSM8K在worst档下表现远弱于MMLU。Temporal C%仅12.4%（worst档cross_benchmark_c_pct_min\n      范围8-14%），扣除permutation null（8.7%）后effective C%仅3.7%——接近noise floor。\n      原因：GSM8K是single-domain math benchmark，items之间homogeneity更高，temporal\n      cohort间的ability差异更直接映射到item difficulty（math能力提升→所有items变容易），\n      MH的ability conditioning更有效地absorb了这个effect。但也可能是GSM8K确实更stable。\n      Semi-synthetic ΔTPR显著降低（worst档0.25-0.4范围），因为smaller item pool（1319 vs 12508）\n      导致power降低，且single-domain matching variable更noisy。\n      GSM1K correlation从registry的-0.478(p=0.005)恶化到-0.29(p=0.10)——在worst档下\n      N=33太小，置信区间覆盖zero。审稿人判定：\"N=33 with CI crossing zero is not evidence\n      for anything\"。Direction仍为negative（与contamination hypothesis相反），\n      但在worst档下这被视为\"noise, not signal\"。GSM1K分析降级为appendix exploratory。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 7: Cross-Benchmark DIF Comparison (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, raw_c_pct, permutation_null, effective_c_pct, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 31.3, 16.4, 14.9, \"moderate signal after controls\"]\n          - [GSM8K, 12.4, 8.7, 3.7, \"near noise floor\"]\n      - title: \"Table 8: GSM1K Correlation Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [metric, value, ci_95, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [Pearson r, -0.29, \"[-0.58, 0.06]\", 0.10]\n          - [Spearman ρ, -0.22, \"[-0.53, 0.14]\", 0.21]\n          - [Partial r, -0.18, \"[-0.50, 0.19]\", 0.32]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: GSM8K permutation null distribution — observed 12.4% barely extends beyond the null range (8.7% mean, SD 1.4%), z=2.6.\"\n      - \"Fig 6: GSM1K scatter plot with wide CI bands crossing zero — visually unconvincing.\"\n    analysis: >\n      GSM8K结果在worst档下严重削弱cross-benchmark generalizability claim。Effective C%=3.7%\n      意味着GSM8K上几乎没有genuine item-level DIF。Reframed paper中，GSM8K从\"cross-benchmark\n      validation\"降级为\"the method produces different results on different benchmarks —\n      this heterogeneity itself is worth characterizing\"。GSM1K correlation完全dropped\n      from claims。\n\n  - name: bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      Pilot bifactor IRT equating on MMLU: fit bifactor model, select anchor items,\n      fixed-parameter calibration of replacements, demonstrate equated score equivalence.\n    expected_results:\n      bifactor_convergence: false\n      bifactor_attempts: 3\n      bifactor_rmsea: 0.089\n      bifactor_cfi: 0.72\n      bifactor_tli: 0.69\n      bifactor_srmr: 0.11\n      fallback_2pl_rmsea: 0.094\n      fallback_2pl_cfi: 0.68\n      anchor_item_selection_possible: false\n      equated_rho: null\n      decision: killed\n      reason: \"bifactor model fails to converge on 12508×5219 matrix; even when forced, fit indices far below acceptable thresholds\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Bifactor IRT在worst档下完全失败。12,508 items × 57 subjects的bifactor model\n      （1 general + 57 specific factors）有>25,000 parameters，在5,219 models上\n      severely overparameterized。Convergence failure after 3 attempts with different\n      starting values和estimation methods（MHRM, EM, QN）。即使forced convergence\n      的fit indices（RMSEA=0.089, CFI=0.72）远低于acceptable thresholds（RMSEA<0.06,\n      CFI>0.95）。这directly confirms审稿人的核心concern：\"unidimensional IRT assumption\n      severely violated, and bifactor doesn't rescue it because the item-to-model ratio\n      is too small for the factor structure\"。Anchor item selection不可能——没有reliable\n      parameter estimates。Equating pilot killed。在worst档下这是paper最致命的finding之一：\n      不仅unidimensional IRT不work，连multidimensional IRT也不work on this data。\n      Reframing response：完全放弃IRT-based interpretation，将MH当作nonparametric test。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 9: IRT Model Fit Comparison\"\n        columns: [model, rmsea, cfi, tli, srmr, converged]\n        rows:\n          - [unidimensional 2PL, 0.094, 0.68, 0.65, 0.12, \"yes (poor fit)\"]\n          - [bifactor (57 specific), 0.089, 0.72, 0.69, 0.11, \"no (forced)\"]\n          - [acceptable thresholds, \"<0.06\", \">0.95\", \">0.95\", \"<0.08\", N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Convergence trace showing parameter oscillation across 3000 EM iterations — no stable solution.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Bifactor failure是worst档的defining event之一。它证实了审稿人的核心concern：\n      MMLU的57-subject structure使得any IRT model都是misspecified的。但在reframed paper中，\n      这反而成为strength：我们explicitly acknowledge IRT assumptions violated，\n      所以我们不依赖IRT interpretation——MH作为nonparametric χ² test不需要IRT model fit。\n      Bifactor结果在limitations section作为\"we attempted and it failed\"报告。\n\n  - name: item_generation_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation\n      with construct constraints. Calibrate via student simulation.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_generated: 200\n      n_items_quality_filtered: 142\n      difficulty_correlation_prompt_based: 0.18\n      difficulty_correlation_student_sim: 0.41\n      difficulty_correlation_target: 0.75\n      construct_alignment_score: 0.64\n      replacement_equating_rho: 0.88\n      replacement_equating_target: 0.95\n      student_sim_correlation_with_actual: 0.52\n      decision: killed_from_main_body\n    result_rationale: >\n      Item generation在worst档下表现远低于target。Prompt-based difficulty targeting\n      几乎无效（ρ=0.18，consistent with literature的0.10-0.45 range低端）。Student\n      simulation calibration有所改善（ρ=0.41）但远低于target 0.75——student simulation\n      on MMLU的multi-domain knowledge items比single-domain math items（arXiv报告的\n      r=0.75-0.82）困难得多。Generated items的construct alignment也不足（0.64），\n      因为MMLU items涵盖highly specialized domain knowledge，LLM generation的semantic\n      equivalence不保证psychometric equivalence。Equating rho=0.88低于0.95 target。\n      在worst档下，整个regeneration pipeline不可行。但这与reframing一致——\n      reframed paper不claim regeneration，而是characterization + toolkit for monitoring。\n      Item generation结果完全dropped，不进appendix（避免给审稿人攻击面）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 10: Difficulty Calibration Methods Comparison\"\n        columns: [method, rho, target, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [prompt-based, 0.18, 0.75, FAIL]\n          - [student simulation, 0.41, 0.75, FAIL]\n          - [combined, 0.47, 0.75, FAIL]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Scatter of target difficulty vs achieved difficulty — massive dispersion, especially for high-difficulty specialized items.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Item generation failure在worst档下是expected的——它依赖于IRT calibration\n      （plan_005已失败）和accurate difficulty prediction（both methods underperform）。\n      从paper中完全删除。\n\n  - name: cumulative_bayesian_dif\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Implement cumulative Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006). Simulate 4\n      successive administrations. Show cumulative power improvement.\n    expected_results:\n      n_simulated_administrations: 4\n      individual_admin_power: 0.40\n      cumulative_2_admin_power: 0.49\n      cumulative_3_admin_power: 0.56\n      cumulative_4_admin_power: 0.61\n      target_cumulative_3_power: 0.70\n      prior_specification_sensitivity: \"results vary 0.48-0.64 across 3 prior choices\"\n      simulation_n_per_admin: 200\n      delta_simulated: 1.0\n      decision: appendix_only\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cumulative Bayesian DIF在worst档下power improvement不达标。3次administration\n      后power仅0.56（target 0.70），4次仅0.61。原因：Sinharay et al.的方法假设successive\n      administrations的examinee populations来自same distribution（exchangeable），\n      但LLM benchmarks中successive cohorts的ability distribution系统性shift（新模型\n      systematically stronger）。Prior accumulation被ability drift corrupted——\n      previous administrations的DIF evidence可能来自ability confound而非genuine item change，\n      累积这些evidence amplifies bias而非reduces noise。Prior specification sensitivity\n      也高（0.48-0.64 range），意味着结果依赖于subjective prior choice。\n      在worst档下，这是simulation-only结果，没有real data validation，审稿人视为\n      underdeveloped。Reframed paper中作为appendix \"future direction\" sketch保留，\n      但不占main body任何空间。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 11: Cumulative DIF Power by Administration Count\"\n        columns: [n_administrations, power, target, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.40, 0.70, -0.30]\n          - [2, 0.49, 0.70, -0.21]\n          - [3, 0.56, 0.70, -0.14]\n          - [4, 0.61, 0.70, -0.09]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Power accumulation curve with 95% CI bands — all below 0.70 target line.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Cumulative Bayesian DIF不达标，但不是blocking issue——reframed paper不依赖\n      longitudinal monitoring power。移至appendix作为future work motivation。\n\n  - name: graceful_degradation_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement.\n      Simulate 5%-50% replacement, measure ranking stability and construct coverage.\n    expected_results:\n      replacement_5pct_rho: 0.998\n      replacement_10pct_rho: 0.994\n      replacement_20pct_rho: 0.981\n      replacement_50pct_rho: 0.937\n      construct_coverage_5pct: 0.97\n      construct_coverage_20pct: 0.88\n      construct_coverage_50pct: 0.71\n      reliability_alpha_original: 0.94\n      reliability_alpha_20pct_replaced: 0.86\n      reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.74\n      theoretical_bound_rho_at_31pct: 0.969\n      decision: appendix_supplementary\n    result_rationale: >\n      Graceful degradation分析在worst档下显示replacement不如预期robust。20% replacement\n      时rho=0.981尚可接受，但reliability从0.94降到0.86——接近educational testing的\n      minimum threshold（0.85）。50% replacement时reliability=0.74，clearly unacceptable。\n      Construct coverage也rapidly degrades——替换items无法maintain MMLU的57-subject\n      knowledge structure。这组结果在worst档下strengthens \"instability ≠ invalidity\"\n      narrative的另一面：removing unstable items 不是好的remediation strategy（at 31%,\n      reliability drops to ~0.85 boundary）。但它也意味着DIF-based benchmark maintenance\n      （audit protocol的\"act\" tier at C%>25）在operational上是risky的。\n      Reframed paper中，这个结果支持\"characterize, don't fix\"的message——\n      用一段话在Discussion中提及，详细数据移appendix。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 12: Graceful Degradation Under Replacement\"\n        columns: [replacement_pct, ranking_rho, reliability_alpha, coverage]\n        rows:\n          - [0, 1.000, 0.94, 1.00]\n          - [5, 0.998, 0.93, 0.97]\n          - [10, 0.994, 0.91, 0.93]\n          - [20, 0.981, 0.86, 0.88]\n          - [31, 0.969, 0.85, 0.82]\n          - [50, 0.937, 0.74, 0.71]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Three-panel degradation curve (rho, alpha, coverage) vs replacement percentage — all show non-linear acceleration past 20%.\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果支持\"monitoring over remediation\"的operational message。在worst档下，\n      直接item removal/replacement不是viable strategy for 31% instability。\n      Reframed paper中作为operational guidance的evidence basis。\n\n  - name: item_focused_trees\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      Implement Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) as alternative to categorical\n      cohort DIF. Treat model release date as continuous covariate.\n    expected_results:\n      ift_implemented: true\n      ift_n_items_flagged: 2847\n      ift_dif_pct: 22.8\n      ift_vs_mh_jaccard: 0.52\n      ift_vs_mh_concordance: 0.71\n      ift_split_points_temporal: \"majority split at 2023-Q3 to 2024-Q1\"\n      ift_nonlinear_dif_detected: 312\n      ift_rmsea_improvement: null\n      ift_advantage: \"avoids arbitrary cohort splits\"\n      ift_disadvantage: \"tree instability — different random seeds yield different splits\"\n      tree_stability_jaccard_across_seeds: 0.63\n      decision: appendix_robustness_check\n    result_rationale: >\n      IFT在worst档下给出与MH partially concordant但不fully consistent的结果。\n      C%=22.8%（低于MH的31.3%），Jaccard=0.52——meaning approximately half the items\n      flagged by each method are unique to that method。IFT的优势（continuous covariate,\n      no arbitrary split）被tree instability抵消——across random seeds的Jaccard仅0.63，\n      意味着IFT结果本身不reproducible。IFT发现312个nonlinear DIF items（difficulty change\n      is non-monotonic over time），这是MH无法detect的，但在worst档下审稿人视为\n      \"additional evidence that the signal is noisy and method-dependent, not that\n      nonlinear DIF is a real phenomenon\"。IFT的split points集中在2023-Q3到2024-Q1，\n      与temporal cohort split大致对齐——这验证了temporal split的合理性，但也意味着\n      IFT没有提供fundamentally new information。在reframed paper中作为appendix\n      robustness check保留，main body一句话提及\"results qualitatively consistent\n      with continuous-covariate alternative\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 13: IFT vs MH-DIF Comparison\"\n        columns: [method, c_pct, unique_flags, overlap_jaccard]\n        rows:\n          - [MH-DIF, 31.3, 1583, 0.52]\n          - [IFT, 22.8, 512, 0.52]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig: Example Item-Focused Tree showing temporal split at 2023-Q4 — qualitatively consistent with binary cohort split.\"\n    analysis: >\n      IFT结果在worst档下是double-edged：支持temporal split的合理性，但method disagreement\n      （Jaccard=0.52）加入审稿人的\"method-dependent results\"narrative。Appendix only。\n\n  - name: architecture_stratified_dif\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      Run DIF within architecture-homogeneous decoder-only subpopulation. Report IRT\n      fit diagnostics. Compare C% and detection power vs full population.\n    expected_results:\n      n_decoder_only: 5226\n      n_non_decoder: 1\n      pct_decoder_only: 99.98\n      decoder_only_c_pct: 31.3\n      decoder_only_jaccard_vs_full: 1.0\n      irt_rmsea_full: 0.094\n      irt_rmsea_decoder_only: 0.094\n      irt_cfi_full: 0.68\n      irt_cfi_decoder_only: 0.68\n      fit_improvement: \"none — removing 1 model changes nothing\"\n      conclusion: \"architecture heterogeneity is not the source of IRT misfit\"\n      real_source_of_misfit: \"57-subject multidimensionality + non-normal ability distribution\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Architecture stratification在worst档下确认了一个重要但trivial的finding：\n      METABENCH MMLU是99.98% decoder-only（5226/5227），removing 1个non-decoder model\n      changes absolutely nothing。C%不变（31.3%），Jaccard=1.0，IRT fit不变。\n      这experiment本身是correct（排除architecture heterogeneity作为concern），\n      但在worst档下审稿人说：\"我们从未argue architecture heterogeneity是问题——问题是\n      57-subject multidimensionality + 非正态ability distribution + model non-independence。\n      你们排除了一个straw man concern\"。IRT fit仍然terrible（RMSEA=0.094, CFI=0.68），\n      因为真正的misfit来源（multidimensionality）没有被addressed。\n      在reframed paper中，architecture homogeneity作为一句话fact（\"METABENCH MMLU is\n      99.98% decoder-only\"）报告，不需要单独实验。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 14: Architecture Stratification (Moot)\"\n        columns: [population, n_models, c_pct, rmsea, cfi]\n        rows:\n          - [full, 5227, 31.3, 0.094, 0.68]\n          - [decoder-only, 5226, 31.3, 0.094, 0.68]\n          - [delta, 1, 0.0, 0.000, 0.00]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      实验本身结论正确（architecture不是问题），但在worst档下被视为wasted space。\n      Reframed paper中压缩为半句话。\n\n  - name: semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\n    plan_id: plan_011\n    description: >\n      Inject known contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure DIF\n      detection power under controlled ground truth. Vary injection parameters.\n    expected_results:\n      n_clean_items_selected: 500\n      n_injected_items: 150\n      temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.39\n      temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.58\n      temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.74\n      temporal_external_tpr_p10: 0.87\n      temporal_external_fpr: 0.318\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p03: 0.07\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.26\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p07: 0.42\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.55\n      ability_external_tpr_p10: 0.62\n      ability_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.19\n      fpr_inflation_at_p10_standard: 0.298_to_0.58\n      matching_variable_contamination: true\n      cross_subject_matching_delta_fpr: 0.003\n      replication_delta_tpr_range: \"[0.25, 0.40]\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Semi-synthetic在worst档下ΔTPR显著低于registry记录。P=0.5时ΔTPR=0.26（registry为\n      0.508），p=1.0时ΔTPR=0.55（registry为0.674）。差异来源：worst档下的injection\n      使用更conservative的parameter choices——injected items选自difficulty分布中间段\n      （避免easy items的ceiling effect），focal group size更接近minimum（N≈100 vs\n      registry的N=807），exploitation rate的effective signal更小（因为\"clean\" baseline\n      items本身已有31%被flag为C-class，diluting the injection signal）。\n      关键问题：baseline FPR=0.318意味着没有injection时就有31.8%的items被flag——\n      ΔTPR必须在这个high baseline上demonstrate增量，signal-to-noise ratio差。\n      Cross-subject matching仍然有效（ΔFPR≈0.003，接近zero），这是anchor finding。\n      但ΔTPR的magnitude（worst档0.25-0.40）审稿人判定为\"moderate at best —\n      the framework works but detection power is underwhelming\"。\n      在reframed paper中，semi-synthetic framework仍是anchor contribution——\n      但framing从\"powerful detection tool\"变为\"principled validation infrastructure\n      with known power limitations\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 15: Semi-Synthetic ΔTPR Under Worst Tier\"\n        columns: [injection_p, tpr, baseline_fpr, delta_tpr, registry_delta_tpr]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 0.39, 0.318, 0.07, 0.222]\n          - [0.5, 0.58, 0.318, 0.26, 0.508]\n          - [0.7, 0.74, 0.318, 0.42, 0.664]\n          - [1.0, 0.87, 0.318, 0.55, 0.674]\n      - title: \"Table 16: Cross-Subject vs Within-Subject Matching\"\n        columns: [matching, delta_fpr, delta_tpr_p05, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [within-subject, \"+0.186\", 0.34, \"FPR inflation — contaminated matching var\"]\n          - [cross-subject, \"+0.003\", 0.26, \"FPR stable — anchor finding preserved\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: Dose-response curve (injection p vs ΔTPR) — monotonic but flatter than registry, reaching 0.55 at p=1.0.\"\n      - \"Fig 9: FPR stability comparison — cross-subject matching maintains ΔFPR≈0 across all injection levels.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Semi-synthetic framework在worst档下power减弱但core innovation（cross-subject matching,\n      ΔFPR≈0）preserved。这成为reframed paper的anchor contribution——framework本身\n      不依赖IRT assumptions，是portable的method contribution。Power limitations\n      honestly reported。\n\n  - name: multi_benchmark_temporal_dif\n    plan_id: plan_028\n    description: >\n      Run temporal DIF on additional benchmarks from METABENCH (ARC, HellaSwag,\n      WinoGrande, TruthfulQA, MMLU-Pro). Address \"only MMLU\" concern.\n    expected_results:\n      mmlu_c_pct: 31.3\n      mmlu_permutation_null: 16.4\n      mmlu_effective: 14.9\n      arc_c_pct: 13.8\n      arc_permutation_null: 9.2\n      arc_effective: 4.6\n      hellaswag_c_pct: 10.1\n      hellaswag_permutation_null: 7.8\n      hellaswag_effective: 2.3\n      winogrande_c_pct: 14.7\n      winogrande_permutation_null: 10.1\n      winogrande_effective: 4.6\n      truthfulqa_c_pct: 22.4\n      truthfulqa_permutation_null: 14.8\n      truthfulqa_effective: 7.6\n      gsm8k_c_pct: 12.4\n      gsm8k_permutation_null: 8.7\n      gsm8k_effective: 3.7\n      cross_benchmark_raw_range: \"10.1-31.3%\"\n      cross_benchmark_effective_range: \"2.3-14.9%\"\n      all_random_controls_below_1pct: true\n      mmlu_pro_not_available: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Multi-benchmark分析在worst档下揭示一个devastating pattern：raw C%在所有benchmarks\n      上都>10%（range 10.1-31.3%），但permutation null也consistently高（7.8-16.4%），\n      扣除后effective C%范围仅2.3-14.9%。MMLU的effective C%最高（14.9%）因为它有最多subjects\n      （57）和最大item pool（12508），提供更多opportunities for heterogeneity。\n      HellaSwag effective C%最低（2.3%），因为it's a relatively homogeneous task\n      （sentence completion）——item-level behavioral heterogeneity genuinely lower。\n      Cross-benchmark heterogeneity本身是informative的（\"different benchmarks have\n      different stability profiles\"），但审稿人concern是：\"if after permutation controls\n      some benchmarks show <5% effective C%, your '31% instability' headline is MMLU-specific\n      and cannot be generalized\"。在worst档下，\"31%\"的headline number必须qualified\n      with \"before permutation controls; effective rate 10-18% depending on benchmark\"。\n      Reframed paper中，cross-benchmark heterogeneity成为characterization的一部分：\n      \"benchmark stability varies from 2% (HellaSwag) to 15% (MMLU) — we provide\n      benchmark-specific profiles\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 17: Multi-Benchmark DIF Summary (Worst Tier)\"\n        columns: [benchmark, n_items, raw_c_pct, permutation_null, effective_c_pct, random_control]\n        rows:\n          - [MMLU, 12508, 31.3, 16.4, 14.9, 0.18]\n          - [TruthfulQA, 817, 22.4, 14.8, 7.6, 0.37]\n          - [WinoGrande, 1267, 14.7, 10.1, 4.6, 0.32]\n          - [ARC, 1172, 13.8, 9.2, 4.6, 0.60]\n          - [GSM8K, 1319, 12.4, 8.7, 3.7, 0.30]\n          - [HellaSwag, 10042, 10.1, 7.8, 2.3, 0.28]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 10: Stacked bar chart: raw C% decomposed into permutation-null component and effective component per benchmark. MMLU dominates; HellaSwag nearly all null.\"\n      - \"Fig 11: Effective C% vs benchmark dimensionality (number of subtopics/categories) — positive correlation, suggesting multi-domain benchmarks show more item heterogeneity.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Multi-benchmark结果在worst档下是mixed news。好消息：all benchmarks show above-chance\n      DIF（random controls <1%）。坏消息：effective signal after permutation controls\n      很小for most benchmarks。Reframed paper必须honest about这个range。\n\n  - name: permutation_null_c_rate\n    plan_id: plan_029\n    description: >\n      1000× permutation test: randomly reassign 2023/2024 temporal labels, run MH-DIF\n      each time. Establish null distribution for C%.\n    expected_results:\n      n_permutations: 1000\n      null_c_pct_mean: 16.4\n      null_c_pct_sd: 2.1\n      null_c_pct_95ci: [12.6, 20.3]\n      null_c_pct_min: 10.8\n      null_c_pct_max: 22.7\n      observed_c_pct: 31.3\n      z_score: 7.1\n      p_value: \"<1e-12\"\n      effective_c_pct: 14.9\n      fraction_spurious: 0.524\n      null_mechanism: \"cohort composition differences (ability, family structure, training vintage) generate substantial DIF even without temporal signal\"\n      random_split_within_cohort_c_pct: 0.18\n      permutation_vs_random_split_gap: \"16.4 vs 0.18 — temporal label permutation preserves between-cohort structure\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Permutation null是worst档的defining experiment。1000次permutation（保持group sizes\n      N_ref=1080, N_foc=807不变，但随机打乱temporal labels）产生mean C%=16.4%（SD=2.1%），\n      95% range [12.6, 20.3]。这意味着即使temporal labels是random的，仅因为两组models\n      的composition差异（ability distribution overlap=76.4%, 不同model families的比例差异,\n      不同training data vintages的representation差异），MH-DIF就会flag 12-20%的items。\n      \n      关键区分：这不是与random-split control（0.18%）矛盾。Random split是within-cohort的\n      （same time period, same family composition），而permutation null是between-cohort的\n      （preserves the actual model composition, just shuffles temporal labels）。\n      The 16.4% null arises because models from 2023 and 2024 genuinely differ in ways\n      beyond temporal signal — model families, training approaches, scale distributions\n      all differ between cohorts. MH's ability conditioning (total score) cannot absorb\n      all these confounds.\n      \n      Observed 31.3% is still z=7.1 above null（p<1e-12），so temporal signal EXISTS\n      beyond cohort composition. But 52.4% of the raw C% is attributable to cohort\n      composition effects, not temporal item-level change. Effective C%=14.9%。\n      \n      在worst档下，审稿人的reaction：\n      \"这证实了我们的concern——31%中一半以上是cohort composition artifact。MH-DIF\n      在LLM context下的conditioning is fundamentally insufficient。14.9%可能也包含\n      未被permutation null capture的confounds（tokenizer changes, training data composition\n      within families）。The genuine temporal item-level signal may be even smaller。\"\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 18: Permutation Null Distribution\"\n        columns: [statistic, value]\n        rows:\n          - [null_mean_c_pct, 16.4]\n          - [null_sd, 2.1]\n          - [null_95_ci, \"[12.6, 20.3]\"]\n          - [observed_c_pct, 31.3]\n          - [z_score, 7.1]\n          - [effective_c_pct, 14.9]\n          - [fraction_spurious, \"52.4%\"]\n          - [random_split_c_pct, 0.18]\n      - title: \"Table 19: Decomposition of Observed C%\"\n        columns: [source, contribution_pct, mechanism]\n        rows:\n          - [genuine_temporal_signal, 14.9, \"item-level behavioral change across model generations\"]\n          - [cohort_composition, 16.4, \"ability distribution + family structure + training vintage differences\"]\n          - [total, 31.3, N/A]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 12: Histogram of 1000 permutation null C% values with observed 31.3% marked. Null distribution is NOT centered at zero — it's centered at 16.4%, far above the random-split baseline of 0.18%.\"\n      - \"Fig 13: Q-Q plot showing null distribution is approximately normal (Shapiro-Wilk p=0.34), validating z-test interpretation.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Permutation null是worst档论文的central finding。它将31%的headline number decompose为\n      ~15% genuine + ~16% spurious。Reframed paper必须lead with这个decomposition：\n      \"we observe 31% raw behavioral heterogeneity, of which approximately half persists\n      after permutation controls — the remainder reflects cohort composition differences\n      that MH-DIF's total-score conditioning cannot absorb\"。这honest framing比\n      原来的\"31% instability\"更defensible，但也更modest。\n\n  - name: odds_ratio_regression_transparency\n    plan_id: plan_030\n    description: >\n      Supplement pseudo R² with odds ratio, CI, McFadden/Nagelkerke R², deviance ratio.\n      Add item-level accuracy change as predictor.\n    expected_results:\n      model1_domain_delta:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0007\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0012\n        or_per_010: 1.55\n        or_ci: [1.19, 2.03]\n      model2_domain_plus_items:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0423\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.072\n        or_domain_per_010: 0.73\n        or_difficulty_per_010: 0.78\n        or_discrimination_per_010: 1.51\n      model3_item_delta:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0012\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0021\n        or_item_change_per_010: 1.08\n        or_item_ci: [1.51, 2.96]\n      model4_full:\n        mcfadden_r2: 0.0434\n        nagelkerke_r2: 0.0737\n        or_item_change_per_010: 0.92\n        or_difficulty_per_010: 0.77\n        or_discrimination_per_010: 1.54\n      simpsons_paradox: true\n      simpsons_direction: \"item accuracy change OR flips from 1.08 to 0.92 when controlling for item properties\"\n      deviance_explained_by_item_props: \"96% of model variance from difficulty + discrimination, not accuracy change\"\n      lr_test_m1_vs_m2_chi2: 647\n      lr_test_m3_vs_m4_chi2: 656\n    result_rationale: >\n      Odds ratio regression在worst档下confirms并extends原有findings。Domain-level\n      accuracy change（Model 1）是significant但tiny predictor（R²=0.0007）。Item-level\n      accuracy change（Model 3）marginally better（R²=0.0012）但still near zero。\n      Simpson's paradox preserved：item accuracy change OR从1.08降到0.92 when controlling\n      for item properties——meaning higher-accuracy-change items are actually LESS likely\n      to be DIF after controlling for difficulty and discrimination。\n      \n      在worst档下，审稿人的worst-case解读：\"item difficulty和discrimination explains 7%\n      of DIF variance（Model 4 R²=0.0737）。这虽然不高in absolute terms，但比accuracy\n      change高50倍。DIF flags与item properties相关——harder, more discriminating items\n      更likely被flag。这可能是MH statistic的statistical property（高discrimination items\n      产生更大的α_MH estimates），而非genuine item-level behavioral change\"。\n      \n      Plan_027的d=-0.17被审稿人认为是marginal的ability gap，但temporal label可能proxy\n      其他未控制confound（training data composition, tokenizer changes, RLHF procedures）。\n      这些confounds不会被total score matching absorb。\n      \n      在reframed paper中，regression transparency section支持honest framing：\"DIF flags\n      are weakly predicted by accuracy change but moderately predicted by item properties —\n      we report this transparently as part of our characterization\"。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Table 20: Logistic Regression Hierarchy\"\n        columns: [model, predictors, mcfadden_r2, nagelkerke_r2, key_or]\n        rows:\n          - [M1, domain_Δacc, 0.0007, 0.0012, \"1.55 [1.19-2.03]\"]\n          - [M2, domain_Δacc + item_props, 0.0423, 0.072, \"0.73 (Δacc flips)\"]\n          - [M3, item_Δacc, 0.0012, 0.0021, \"1.08\"]\n          - [M4, item_Δacc + item_props, 0.0434, 0.0737, \"0.92 (Δacc flips)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 14: Simpson's paradox visualization — marginal OR for accuracy change is >1 (DIF-promoting), but conditional OR is <1 (DIF-protective) after item property control.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Regression transparency strengthens honest framing但也gives审稿人ammunition：\n      \"item properties explain 50× more variance than accuracy change — DIF may be\n      a statistical artifact of item difficulty/discrimination structure\"。\n      Reframed paper must address this directly。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"03381ec8-53c9-4c55-86f7-a45910704277","total_cost_usd":0.6451905,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24168,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":18759,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24168,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":18759,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24168},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":19130,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.019235000000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":18759,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24168,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6259555,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"50dcdd8c-f9a8-4baf-951b-0d23570e8161"}
